      <a href="/teachings/likutay-moharan" class="nav-link">← Index</a>
      <a href="/teachings/likutay-moharan-volume-1-torah-257" class="nav-link">Next →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</nav>

<section class="content">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-text">
      <p><strong>256</strong><strong> </strong><strong>-</strong><strong> </strong><strong>The</strong><strong> </strong><strong>Name</strong><strong> </strong><strong>אתה</strong><strong> </strong><strong>(You)</strong><strong> </strong><strong>is</strong><strong> </strong><strong>a</strong><strong> </strong><strong><em>segula</em></strong><strong> </strong><strong>over</strong><strong> </strong><strong>the</strong><strong> </strong><strong>sea</strong></p>
      <p>The Name אתה (You) is a <em>segula</em> [propitious] over the sea, to subdue the waves (See Chayay Moharan - The Life of Our Leader Rabbi Nachman 136, and Parparos Lichuchmah), and the secret is <strong>"In</strong><strong> </strong><strong>the</strong><strong> </strong><strong>rising</strong><strong> </strong><strong>of</strong><strong> </strong><strong>its</strong><strong> </strong><strong>waves</strong><strong> </strong><strong>You</strong><strong> </strong><strong>(</strong><strong>אתה</strong><strong>)</strong><strong> </strong><strong>calm</strong><strong> </strong><strong>them"</strong> [<em>Psalms</em> 89:10] (see Zohar Noach 69 and in Mikdash Melech there [referring to Kabbalistic sources explaining divine names as protections]).</p>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

